# Existing starter strategies

These notes describe existing in-game starter themes. Verify exact current card IDs with tools before using a list.

# Core starter decks

The five improved lists formerly named V2 now replace their original versions. The source starter roster contains one Burn Bright, Ice Current, Rocket Current, Garden Furnace and Dragon Tempest, plus the two mascot, ten Legendary-theme and two [Water and Grass decks](element-starter-decks.md): 19 before the latest Dragon additions. [Dragon's Ascent](dragon-ascent-deck.md) and [Axe Forge](axe-forge-deck.md) bring the current Windows quick-build roster to 21. The Water and Grass additions are included in the current Windows quick build. Starter previews now use the actual featured Pokémon card with the automatic supporting fan; decorated custom covers are no longer loaded. Ice Current and Dragon Tempest now use the balance-tested lists described below.

Their canonical IDs are `showdown-fire`, `showdown-water`, `showdown-bridge`, `showdown-mixed` and `showdown-dragon`. Previous `-v2` IDs resolve to these decks for compatibility but are not listed as separate starters. Existing saved custom deck copies are independent and are not deleted or rewritten.

| Deck | Identity and changes | Pokémon / Trainers / Energy |
|---|---|---|
| Burn Bright | Charizard doubles Fire Energy for Magmortar's heavy attacks; Entei supplies Burn. More evolution search and recovery support rotating attackers. | 17 / 30 / 13 |
| Ice Current | Ice Dance Frosmoth prepares the Bench and Articuno gathers Energy. Three Pokémon 151 Lapras offer Aqua Edge and Basic search; two Mantine support setup. Irida finds a Water Pokémon and an Item. | 17 / 29 / 14 |
| Rocket Current | Vaporeon pressures ex/V while Weezing suppresses Abilities and Yveltal traps the Active. Judge, Counter Catcher and Crushing Hammer reinforce disruption. | 18 / 29 / 13 |
| Garden Furnace | Cherrim and Charizard jointly power Scovillain's Grass/Fire attack. Tapu Bulu supplies a powerful secondary attack. This deck relies on Trainer draw rather than Bibarel. | 18 / 28 / 14 |
| Dragon Tempest | One Salamence ex spreads damage for two single-prize Salamence with Fierce Dragon. Two Rare Candy speed evolution and three Crispin supply mixed Energy. Druddigon and Rayquaza support the attackers. | 16 / 30 / 14 |

Each deck contains one copy of its thematic Legendary. All use the project's
Modern practice pool, rather than official current Standard rotation. The
picker uses actual Pokémon card scans on the featured stack. Supporting cards,
type accents and summaries are configured in
`unity/PokemonTCG/Assets/StreamingAssets/UI/StarterDecks/deck-art.json`.

Definitions are in `ShowdownDecks.cs`. Runtime printing replacement selects the currently active printing without changing quantities.

The old generated cover images are historical assets; the game no longer uses image overrides.

## Applied balance changes (2026-10-05)

The final seven-deck experiment in `reports/simulations/seven-decks-dragon-buff-500-20261005/` ran 500 games per pairing. Its lists are now applied to the canonical starters:

- Ice Current removes Freezing Chill Frosmoth and replaces its previous three Lapras with three `sv3pt5-131` Lapras; Mantine increases from one to two. Three Ice Dance Frosmoth remain.
- Dragon Tempest reduces Shelgon from three to two and Salamence ex from three to one, adds two `swsh7-109` Salamence, two Rare Candy and three Crispin, removes both Level Ball and the Energy Search, and reduces Energy Retrieval from three to two.
- Pika Power changes from three Thunderbolt Raichu / one Strong Volt Raichu to one / three; see the mascot guide.

Burn Bright, Rocket Current, Garden Furnace, Eevee's Rainbow and the ten newer theme decks retain their lists. The seven-deck experiment put Dragon at 50.5% mean win rate and Ice Current at 48.4%; Pika at 59.7% and Garden at 40.9% still need further balancing. These are AI estimates against the six other tested decks, not predictions for the expanded 17-deck roster or human play. Application evidence is under `reports/starter-balance-applied-20261005/`.

## Consolidation verification before balance changes

The consolidation build passed all 5,384 native scenarios and the simulator self-tests. Desktop (1672×941) and smaller-window (1100×800) picker runs each passed 892 checks with no text overflow, including exact template copies, retained covers, paging, Random, Undo, persistence and battle selection. At that milestone, the retained five lists were compared against their pre-rename V2 definitions and were unchanged. Evidence: `reports/starter-consolidation/acceptance.json`.

