# Dragon's Ascent

A second Dragon-themed Modern practice starter, ID `showdown-ascent`. The deck uses 19 Pokémon, 27 Trainers and 14 Basic Energy: 60 cards total. It includes exactly one Legendary copy, Zekrom. The existing 19 starters are unchanged, giving 20 in source at its introduction. [Axe Forge](axe-forge-deck.md) subsequently raised the source roster to 21.

## Strategy

Build Dratini into Dragonair, whose Evolutionary Guidance finds Evolution Pokémon when it has Energy attached. Two Jet Cruise Dragonite give your Pokémon free retreat and attack for 180 with Water and Lightning Energy. Their Dragon Pulse discards the top two cards of your deck, so manage the remaining deck carefully.

Eelektrik's Dynamotor attaches discarded Basic Lightning Energy to a Benched Pokémon. Use Ultra Ball or Professor's Research to put Lightning Energy in the discard, then move a charged attacker forward. Crispin finds two different Basic Energy types and attaches one, helping meet the mixed Water/Lightning costs.

The third Dragonite uses Energy Hurricane: 180 damage plus up to three Basic Energy attachments from the deck. It costs four Energy, giving a heavier option that prepares the next attacker. Zekrom's Wild Shock deals 130 and Paralyzes the opponent, but deals 60 to itself; three consecutive uses without healing would Knock it Out. Bibarel supports drawing, while Super Rod recycles Pokémon and Basic Energy.

Retreat is still limited to once per turn, even with Jet Cruise. Free retreat does not remove status or effect restrictions that prevent retreat. Keep the single Switch for those situations.

This deck focuses on mobility and Energy recovery; Dragon Tempest retains its Salamence and Bench-damage strategy. Zekrom is a Legendary Pokémon with a Lightning-type card in this Dragon-themed deck. The list uses the game's active Modern practice pool, not official Standard rotation.

