# Axe Forge

A separate Haxorus-themed Modern practice starter, ID `showdown-forge`. It uses 19 Pokémon, 26 Trainers and 15 Basic Energy: 60 cards total. There is exactly one Legendary copy, Dialga. The source roster is now 21, with the previous 20 starter lists unchanged.

## Strategy

Start with Axew's Gather Strength to find Basic Energy, then evolve through Fraxure to Haxorus or use Rare Candy. Two Haxorus have Dragon Pulse for 230 damage at a Fighting + Metal cost. Bring Down the Axe can Knock Out an opponent whose Active Pokémon has Special Energy attached. The third Haxorus has Cross-Cut for 160 against Evolution Pokémon, or Axe Blast to Knock Out a Basic Pokémon at a Fighting + Metal + Colorless cost. Each effect remains subject to applicable defending effects.

Metang's Metal Maker looks at four cards and attaches the Basic Metal Energy found there to your Pokémon, putting the others on the bottom of your deck. Nine Metal Energy support this engine; six Fighting Energy and three Crispin help supply Haxorus's other cost. Beldum's Call for Family finds Basic Pokémon, while Bibarel supports drawing. Switch rotates attackers.

Dragon Pulse discards the top three cards of your deck. Watch the deck count: repeated attacks and drawing can cause deck-out. Dialga's Temporal Backflow recovers one discarded card to hand instead of dealing damage; its Metal Blast grows stronger with attached Metal Energy. Two Super Rod recycle Pokémon and Basic Energy into the deck.

The full Axew → Fraxure → Haxorus line is 4–3–3. This deck uses **only Fighting and Metal Energy**, so it does not require mixing Dragon's Ascent's Water and Lightning Energy into the same list. Haxorus is a Dragon-type card; Dialga's selected printing is Metal. These are supported Modern practice cards, not an official Standard-rotation list.

